    "what_happens_next": {
      "type": "output",
      "name": "What Happens Next",
      "metadata": {},
      "channel": "transcript",
      "message": "We'll update your claim with the new information you provided. \r\n\r\nWe aim to do this within 10 working days. After we've updated your information, we'll let you know if you're due a payment. \r\n\r\nIf you're updating your: \r\n\r\n* name\r\n* National Insurance number \r\n* date of birth\r\n\r\nYou'll need to email a copy of your driving licence, passport and/or wage slip, quoting your claim reference number (LN12345678) to:\r\n\r\n[redundancypaymentsonline@insolvency.gov.uk (opens in new tab)](mailto:redundancypaymentsonline@insolvency.gov.uk)\r\n\r\nOtherwise, you do not need to send any further evidence to complete your application.\r\n\r\nIf you do not get a response from us within 15 working days, contact: [redundancypaymentsonline@insolvency.gov.uk](mailto:redundancypaymentsonline@insolvency.gov.uk)\r\n\r\nMake sure you tell the insolvency practitioner handling your employer’s insolvency about any changes you make to your claim. They may need to update the information they provide to the Insolvency Service.\r\n\r\nTo make another amendment, complete the relevant form on the [redundancy claim amendment forms](https://www.gov.uk/guidance/amend-a-redundancy-claim) page.",
      "on_error": "fail",
      "next": "end_process"
